WHY IT IS WRITTEN THIS WAY
--------------------------

Licensing is one of the few decisions in this repository that cannot be
undone. Code released under a permissive licence stays released under it:
that commit can be forked, rebranded, and sold, forever, with no recourse.
Restrictive terms can always be loosened later. The reverse is impossible.

So the terms start closed and deliberately un-final, to be settled before the
first public release rather than by accident on the first push.

Note that this says nothing about what Timbre costs its users. The product is
free, runs entirely on-device, and requires no account (GDR-0001). That is a
promise about price and privacy, not about source licensing, and the two are
independent.

See docs/decisions/gdr/0005-licensing-preserves-optionality.md.
